|ECR image pull failure due to Execution Role misconfiguration|🟢 Low   |Low                |Validated in PoC. Policies are templated. Add ECR pull validation to CI pipeline for task definition changes.      |
|VPC/NAT connectivity issues                                  |🟢 Low   |Low                |Validated in PoC. Recommend VPC endpoints for ECR and S3 to eliminate NAT Gateway dependency entirely.             |
|Step Functions does not handle task failure gracefully       |🟡 Medium|Low                |Implement explicit error/retry states in the state machine. Define alerting on task failure exit codes.            |

📄 7.1 — Migration Plan (Phased)
Labels: migration plan rollout phases
Parent: Migration & Rollout

Overview
The migration is structured into four phases over six weeks, with a parallel-running phase to validate correctness before full cutover.

Phase 1 — Foundation (Week 1–2)
Goal: Make all tenants Fargate-ready without touching production execution.
	∙	Finalise Fargate task definition template for all active tenants
	∙	Update Service Catalog product to deploy Fargate-compatible task definitions
	∙	Validate VPC endpoints for ECR and S3
	∙	Update IAM role templates (SM IAM Role, ECS Task IAM Role, Execution Role) across all tenants
	∙	Update SSM parameter paths if required

Phase 2 — Parallel Running (Week 3–4)
Goal: Validate Fargate output parity against EC2 with zero production risk.
	∙	Select two pilot tenants for parallel running
	∙	Run DBT jobs on both EC2 and Fargate paths simultaneously for pilot tenants
	∙	Compare output correctness, execution time, and log completeness
	∙	Monitor CloudWatch metrics: task launch time, execution duration, failure rate
	∙	Sign off from pilot tenant owners

Phase 3 — Full Cutover (Week 5–6)
Goal: Migrate all tenants to Fargate; decommission EC2 infrastructure.
	∙	Migrate all remaining tenants to Fargate launch type
	∙	Confirm all tenants’ DBT runs executing correctly on Fargate
	∙	Drain and deregister EC2 instances from the ECS cluster
	∙	Delete Auto Scaling Group, launch templates, and associated EC2 resources
	∙	Deregister and deprecate old EC2-based AMIs
	∙	Update all runbooks and operational documentation

Phase 4 — Optimisation (Post-Migration)
Goal: Extract maximum value from the Fargate model.
	∙	Enable Fargate Spot for non-critical / dev tenants
	∙	Add per-tenant cost tagging to all Fargate task definitions
	∙	Right-size CPU/memory per tenant based on actual run metrics
	∙	Implement Step Functions retry and error-handling states
	∙	Set up cost attribution dashboard in AWS Cost Explorer by tenant tag

📄 7.2 — Runbook: Deploying a New Tenant on Fargate
Labels: runbook onboarding tenant operations
Parent: Migration & Rollout

Prerequisites
	∙	Tenant ID confirmed
	∙	Nexus image URL provided
	∙	Target data warehouse credentials available in Secrets Manager or SSM
	∙	Subnets and security groups identified for the tenant

Steps
Step 1 — Create IAM Roles
	∙	Deploy SM IAM Role for Step Functions (use tenant-scoped template)
	∙	Deploy ECS Task IAM Role (scope S3, SSM, CloudWatch to tenant resources)
	∙	Deploy ECS Execution Role (scope ECR and CloudWatch only)
Step 2 — Create ECR Repository
	∙	Create tenant ECR repository
	∙	Configure Nexus sync to push the DBT image to tenant ECR
Step 3 — Create Task Definition
	∙	Use Fargate task definition template
	∙	Set requiresCompatibilities: FARGATE
	∙	Set networkMode: awsvpc
	∙	Assign Task IAM Role and Execution Role ARNs
	∙	Configure CPU and memory (baseline: 1 vCPU / 2GB; tune per tenant)
	∙	Set CloudWatch log group path to tenant log group
Step 4 — Store Task Definition ARN in SSM
	∙	Register the task definition
	∙	Store the ARN at the tenant SSM parameter path
Step 5 — Create CloudWatch Log Group
	∙	Create tenant-scoped log group
	∙	Set retention policy
Step 6 — Deploy State Machine
	∙	Deploy Step Functions state machine using the tenant SM IAM Role
	∙	Configure ECS RunTask action with tenant subnets and security groups
Step 7 — Deploy Service Catalog Product
	∙	Create ECS-TASK Service Catalog product for the tenant
	∙	Wire to the State Machine ARN
	∙	Set accepted parameters: TaskDefinitionSSM, SynchNexusImage
Step 8 — Validate
	∙	Trigger a test DBT run via Service Catalog
	∙	Verify task reaches RUNNING state
	∙	Verify CloudWatch logs are streaming
	∙	Verify S3 outputs are written
	∙	Verify task reaches STOPPED with exit code 0

📄 8.1 — Glossary
Labels: reference glossary
Parent: Reference



|Term           |Definition                                                                                                   |
|---------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|DBT            |Data Build Tool — open-source framework for running SQL-based data transformations in the warehouse          |
|ECS            |Amazon Elastic Container Service — AWS managed container orchestration platform                              |
|Fargate        |AWS serverless compute engine for containers — no EC2 instances to provision or manage                       |
|ENI            |Elastic Network Interface — a virtual network card; each Fargate task receives a dedicated ENI in awsvpc mode|
|State Machine  |AWS Step Functions workflow that orchestrates the DBT execution sequence                                     |
|Service Catalog|AWS service enabling self-service deployment of pre-approved architecture products by tenants                |
|Task Definition|ECS configuration specifying container image, CPU, memory, network mode, IAM roles, and environment variables|
|ECR            |Amazon Elastic Container Registry — managed Docker container image registry                                  |
|SSM            |AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store — key-value store for configuration values like task definition ARNs     |
|ASG            |Auto Scaling Group — EC2 fleet management mechanism; eliminated in the Fargate model                         |
|AMI            |Amazon Machine Image — EC2 instance OS snapshot; not required with Fargate                                   |
|awsvpc         |ECS network mode that assigns a dedicated ENI to each task — mandatory for Fargate                           |
|SM IAM Role    |The IAM role assumed by Step Functions to invoke ECS RunTask and pass the ECS Task IAM Role                  |
|Execution Role |The IAM role used by Fargate to pull container images from ECR and stream logs to CloudWatch                 |
|Task IAM Role  |The IAM role assumed by the running container — defines what the DBT code can access at runtime              |
|Fargate Spot   |Discounted Fargate capacity that can be interrupted — suitable for non-critical workloads                    |
|PoC            |Proof of Concept — a working prototype validating the feasibility of the proposed architecture               |

